 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Bonus Exercise: Combine Embeddings & LLM API\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective**: Combine both exercises to create an intelligent prompt selection system.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Workflow**:\n",
    "1. Generate embeddings for multiple candidate prompts\n",
    "2. Calculate similarity with a reference query\n",
    "3. Select the most similar/relevant prompt\n",
    "4. Send only the best-matching query to the LLM\n",
    "5. Display and analyze results\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning Outcomes**:\n",
    "- Combine embeddings and API calls\n",
    "- Implement intelligent query routing\n",
    "- Optimize API usage and costs\n",
    "- Understand semantic similarity in practice"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 1: Import Libraries & Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load environment variables\n",
    "load_dotenv()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ All libraries imported successfully\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 2: Load Models"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load SentenceTransformer model\n",
    "model = SentenceTransformer('all-MiniLM-L6-v2')\n",
    "print(\"✓ SentenceTransformer model loaded\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load API configuration\n",
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = os.getenv('ANTHROPIC_API_KEY')\n",
    "API_URL = \"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\"\n",
    "MODEL = \"claude-3-5-haiku-20241022\"\n",
    "\n",
    "if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:\n",
    "    print(\"✓ Anthropic API configured\")\n    "For valid API key\")\n    else:\n",
    "    print(\"❌ ERROR: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not found in .env\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 3: Define Reference Query & Candidate Prompts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Reference query - what we're looking for\n",
    "reference_query = \"Explain how machine learning works\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Reference Query: '{reference_query}'\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Multiple candidate prompts with different semantic meanings\n",
    "candidate_prompts = [\n",
    "    \"What is supervised learning?\",\n",
    "    \"How do neural networks function?\",\n",
    "    \"Explain machine learning and its algorithms\",\n",
    "    \"What are the best programming languages?\",\n",
    "    \"How does deep learning differ from traditional ML?\",\n",
    "    \"Tell me about cricket rules\",\n",
    "    \"What is artificial intelligence?\",\n",
    "    \"Describe natural language processing\",\n",
    "    \"How can I improve my cooking skills?\",\n",
    "    \"What are the applications of machine learning?\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate Prompts ({len(candidate_prompts)}):\")\n",
    "for i, prompt in enumerate(candidate_prompts, 1):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {i}. {prompt}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 4: Generate Embeddings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate embedding for reference query\n",
    "ref_embedding = model.encode(reference_query, convert_to_tensor=True)\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Reference query embedding generated\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Dimension: {ref_embedding.shape[0]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  First 5 values: {ref_embedding[:5].tolist()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate embeddings for all candidate prompts\n",
    "candidate_embeddings = model.encode(candidate_prompts, convert_to_tensor=True)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n✓ Candidate prompts embeddings generated\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total prompts: {len(candidate_prompts)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Shape: {candidate_embeddings.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 5: Calculate Similarity Scores"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert to numpy\n",
    "ref_emb_np = ref_embedding.cpu().numpy() if hasattr(ref_embedding, 'cpu') else np.array(ref_embedding)\n",
    "cand_emb_np = candidate_embeddings.cpu().numpy() if hasattr(candidate_embeddings, 'cpu') else np.array(candidate_embeddings)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate similarity between reference and all candidates\n",
    "similarities = cosine_similarity([ref_emb_np], cand_emb_np)[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Similarity scores calculated\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Average similarity: {np.mean(similarities):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Max similarity: {np.max(similarities):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Min similarity: {np.min(similarities):.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 6: Rank Prompts by Similarity"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create list of (prompt, similarity) tuples\n",
    "prompt_scores = list(zip(candidate_prompts, similarities))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by similarity (descending)\n",
    "prompt_scores_sorted = sorted(prompt_scores, key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(\"SIMILARITY RANKING\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display all scores with color coding\n",
    "for i, (prompt, score) in enumerate(prompt_scores_sorted, 1):\n",
    "    if score > 0.7:\n",
    "        emoji = \"🟢\"\n",
    "        level = \"Very High\"\n",
    "    elif score > 0.5:\n",
    "        emoji = \"🟡\"\n",
    "        level = \"High\"\n",
    "    elif score > 0.3:\n",
    "        emoji = \"🟠\"\n",
    "        level = \"Moderate\"\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        emoji = \"🔴\"\n",
    "        level = \"Low\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"{emoji} {i:2d}. [{score:.4f}] {level:10s} | {prompt}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 7: Select Best Matching Prompt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "best_prompt = prompt_scores_sorted[0][0]\n",
    "best_score = prompt_scores_sorted[0][1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(\"BEST MATCH SELECTED\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n🏆 Selected Prompt:\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Text: '{best_prompt}'\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Similarity Score: {best_score:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Confidence: {best_score * 100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTop 3 Alternatives:\")\n",
    "for i in range(1, min(4, len(prompt_scores_sorted))):\n",
    "    prompt, score = prompt_scores_sorted[i]\n",
    "    print(f\"   {i}. [{score:.4f}] {prompt}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 8: Define LLM API Function"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def call_llm_api(user_query, temperature=0.7, max_tokens=512):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Send query to Claude Haiku API\"\"\"\n",
    "    headers = {\n",
    "        \"x-api-key\": ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,\n",
    "        \"anthropic-version\": \"2023-06-01\",\n",
    "        \"content-type\": \"application/json\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    payload = {\n",
    "        \"model\": MODEL,\n",
    "        \"max_tokens\": max_tokens,\n",
    "        \"temperature\": temperature,\n",
    "        \"messages\": [\n",
    "            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_query}\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        response = requests.post(API_URL, headers=headers, json=payload, timeout=30)\n",
    "        response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "        return response.json()\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        return {\"error\": str(e)}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ API function defined\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 9: Send Best Prompt to LLM"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"\\n{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "print(\"SENDING TO LLM\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSending prompt to Claude Haiku...\")\n",
    "print(f\"Prompt: '{best_prompt}'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Call the LLM with the best matching prompt\n",
    "response = call_llm_api(best_prompt, temperature=0.7, max_tokens=512)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Response received from LLM!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 10: Display LLM Response"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"\\n{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "print(\"LLM RESPONSE\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if \"error\" in response:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n❌ ERROR: {response['error']}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    if \"content\" in response and len(response[\"content\"]) > 0:\n",
    "        reply = response[\"content\"][0][\"text\"]\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n{reply}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        if \"usage\" in response:\n",
    "            print(f\"\\n{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "            print(\"Token Usage:\")\n",
    "            print(f\"  Input tokens: {response['usage']['input_tokens']}\")\n",
    "            print(f\"  Output tokens: {response['usage']['output_tokens']}\")\n",
    "            print(f\"  Total: {response['usage']['input_tokens'] + response['usage']['output_tokens']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Block 11: Semantic Clustering Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Categorize by similarity level\n",
    "very_high = sum(1 for _, s in prompt_scores_sorted if s > 0.7)\n",
    "high = sum(1 for _, s in prompt_scores_sorted if 0.5 <= s <= 0.7)\n",
    "moderate = sum(1 for _, s in prompt_scores_sorted if 0.3 <= s <= 0.5)\n",
    "low = sum(1 for _, s in prompt_scores_sorted if s < 0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "print(\"SEMANTIC CLUSTERING\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'=' * 80}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Distribution:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  🟢 Very High (>0.7):  {very_high} prompts\")\n",
    "print(f\"  🟡 High (0.5-0.7):    {high} prompts\")\n",
    "print(f\"  🟠 Moderate (0.3-0.5): {moderate} prompts\")\n",
    "print(f\"  🔴 Low (<0.3):        {low} prompts\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create visualization table\n",
    "df_data = []\n",
    "for i, (prompt, score) in enumerate(prompt_scores_sorted, 1):\n",
    "    if score > 0.7:\n",
    "        category = \"Very High\"\n",
    "    elif score > 0.5:\n",
    "        category = \"High\"\n",
    "    elif score > 0.3:\n",
    "        category = \"Moderate\"\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        category = \"Low\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    df_data.append({\n",
    "        'Rank': i,\n",
    "        'Prompt': prompt,\n",
    "        'Score': f\"{score:.4f}\",\n",
    "        'Category': category\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(df_data)\n",
    "print(f\"\\n{df.to_string(index=False)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
